Author:     wenjinhust <33047235+wenjinhust@users.noreply.github.com>
AuthorDate: Mon Oct 12 20:21:59 2026 +0800
Commit:     GitHub <noreply@github.com>
CommitDate: Mon Oct 12 20:21:59 2026 +0800

    [BugFix][Doc] Delete the usage of jemalloc (#18392)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    - Fixes #18377
    
    - Delete the usage of jemalloc from the Ascend plugin:
    - Remove the `LD_PRELOAD=libjemalloc.so.2` injection from all
    Dockerfiles (`Dockerfile`, `Dockerfile.310p`,
    `Dockerfile.310p.openEuler`, `Dockerfile.a3`, `Dockerfile.a3.openEuler`,
    `Dockerfile.a5`, `Dockerfile.a5.openEuler`, `Dockerfile.openEuler`)
    - Remove the `jemalloc` / `libjemalloc2` package from CI system
    dependency installation and image builds
    - Remove the `LD_PRELOAD` env and related jemalloc references from docs,
    e2e case configs, and `test_minimax_m3.py`
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    - No. Users are no longer required to preload `libjemalloc.so.2`; the
    plugin no longer relies on jemalloc.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - CI build of the Ascend Docker images (all build types and OS variants)
    - Unit tests: `pytest tests/`
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/8cc9aa5ad350f6f80cf3bebb298d410803ff75a9
    
    Signed-off-by: wenjinhust <wenjin.sh@huawei.com>

